From 49d4adac5ca6baab4989d3ed6216ed00f9a21375 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrik Eriksson <patrik.m.eriksson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:27:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] media: trim after a delete made outside Core, and after
 every pre-roll clip delete

Why: Core trims the drive after its own deletes that free 1 GiB or more, but the touch UI
deletes clips itself (Apertar-UI cliplistmodel.cpp removes the files directly; Core has no
delete socket command the UI could call), so a shooting day driven from the touch UI never
trims and the stall after about 0.9 TB of writing can come back. The storage pre-roll deletes
0.7 to 1.5 GB per run, below the threshold for 16-bit Clear HDR and lossless takes, right
before the operator's first take. Found by the kb's research (working/dng-chain, R4; verified
in V/H6).

What: the media watcher asks for a trim when the mounted medium gains 1 GiB or more between two
polls while nothing records and no Core delete runs (reason "free-space"); the pre-roll always
asks for one after it removes its clip. Both go through the existing idle-only trim worker and
coalesce with pending requests. Cost: on exFAT every fstrim re-discards all free space, so a
mount now runs two or three full trims (0.47 s each measured) before the first take.

Tested: the file syntax-checks on the host. Reviewed (V/PATCHES.md): a format cannot trigger it
(the medium is unmounted); one-by-one deletes below 1 GiB each do not. Not run on the Pi: delete
a clip from the touch UI and expect "media: trim ... reason=free-space" in the journal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1zNNwfkFFgzHEzb7wV
---
 src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
index 95d0766..e58a43d 100644
--- a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
+++ b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
@@ -10464,6 +10464,13 @@ void ApertarCoreApp::runMediaWatcher()
             mediaSnapshot_ = current;
             mediaSnapshotValid_ = true;
         }
+        // A delete made outside Core (the touch UI removes clips itself) frees space without a trim: when the
+        // mounted medium gains 1 GiB or more between two polls while nothing records, ask for one. Core's own
+        // deletes already request theirs; repeated requests coalesce (kb working/dng-chain, R4).
+        if (havePrevious && current.mounted() && previous.mounted() && current.sameMedium(previous) &&
+            current.freeBytes > previous.freeBytes && current.freeBytes - previous.freeBytes >= (1ULL << 30) &&
+            !camera_.isRecording() && !mediaDeleteActive_.load())
+            trimMedia("free-space");
         if (!havePrevious || !current.sameMedium(previous)) {
             std::cerr << "ApertarCore media: state=" << current.stateName()
                       << " device=" << current.device << " fstype=" << current.fstype
@@ -10866,8 +10873,9 @@ void ApertarCoreApp::runStoragePrerollOnce(storagepreroll::Trigger trigger, unsi
     }
     storagepreroll::prerollState().fps.store(0.0, std::memory_order_release);
     storagepreroll::prerollState().active.store(false, std::memory_order_release);
-    if (result.bytes >= (1ULL << 30))
-        trimMedia("delete");   // the delete freed 1 GiB or more: the usual trim, now that the medium is free again
+    // The deleted clip (0.7 GB at 4K lossless, 1.4 GB at 4K 12-bit 60 fps) would otherwise sit untrimmed under the
+    // next take; the trim is quick (927 GB in 0.47 s measured) and runs only while the medium is idle.
+    trimMedia("delete");
 }
 
 MediaSnapshot ApertarCoreApp::mediaSnapshot() const
